ent-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:6c284097e681979f17d222f50d673084ad1a7a075e22d13b2b15a4d1fbfb141c","file":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":30,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"4e3fcfbe53344dcc9af071c52cb3d0a5297d34d9ffa2cde9102509f6d8e92900","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:6c284097e681979f17d222f50d673084ad1a7a075e22d13b2b15a4d1fbfb141c","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L30"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{fac:main}\nThere are absolute constants $\\eta,c,C>0$ such that, with $a=1/1000$,\n\\[\n \\log\\E_{y\\sim u_{N,k}}R_x(y)^{1+a}\n \\le Ck(k/N)^\\eta\n \\qquad(1\\le k\\le N),\n\\]\nuniformly over every starting injection $x$. For every sufficiently\nlarge dyadic $N$ and every nontrivial irreducible representation,\n\\[\n T_N(\\lambda)=0\\quad\\hbox{or}\\quad\n \\|T_N(\\lambda)\\|_{\\op}\\le D_\\lambda^{-c}.\n\\]\nConsequently an absolute number of forward sweeps has worst-start\ntotal-variation distance from uniform tending to zero as $d\\to\\infty$."}
